  "details": "I found it's pretty strange to see why my avatar is not already loaded when move to other room. \n\nThe reason is simple: my avatar is still same when move to other room, and it's already stored in cache. But i can see it needs at least 5-10 (or even 15) seconds before my blue preload avatar goes away.\nWhy is blue avatar showed already there? Because it can show it immediately. Why just not show immediately my avatar instead the blue preload avatar?\n\nRooms are stored in cache, so if you come fast back to same room, you can see it's loading fast and you're in the room. But avatars, for strange reason, if you come fast back, all avatars are loading again.\n\nIt doesn't make sense why it cannot show immediately my avatar. Especially streamers who jumped to many rooms, they're forced to wait first for 5-10-15 sec before own avatar appear and can move further.\n\nI have feel the avatars have missing checksum code for changes inside avatar. If you upload avatar to the server, it has new checksum code. The avatar ID is still same. The checksum code should also stored in cache with avatar. So it can verify if the avatar is unchanged, it will use the cache - so it will load much faster and faster ready to make it visible in the room.\n\nAnd if you block some avatar parts like shader and animation, should it just use cached avatar and load it without shaders? That should faster ready, but i don't know how system worked in VRChat. Technically said, avatars in cache should faster loaded and showed in the world when you re-enter same room again.",
